<p>The expo runs alongside the summit and opens fully on day three. It is not a general trade fair — the audience is the delegate list, which means the people walking your stand are the buyers, investors and processors who registered for the forums.</p>

<h2>What can be exhibited</h2>

<ul class="classes">
  <li class="class-row">
    <span class="class-row__code">Class 1</span>
    <span class="class-row__name">Tea products</span>
    <p>Black, green, orthodox, speciality, purple, blended and branded lines. Finished goods and bulk.</p>
  </li>
  <li class="class-row">
    <span class="class-row__code">Class 2</span>
    <span class="class-row__name">Processing equipment</span>
    <p>Withering, rolling, oxidation, drying, sorting, grading and packing machinery.</p>
  </li>
  <li class="class-row">
    <span class="class-row__code">Class 3</span>
    <span class="class-row__name">Agricultural technologies</span>
    <p>Inputs, irrigation, mechanised plucking, soil and yield analytics, traceability systems.</p>
  </li>
  <li class="class-row">
    <span class="class-row__code">Class 4</span>
    <span class="class-row__name">Logistics services</span>
    <p>Freight, warehousing, cold chain, customs and export documentation.</p>
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Why exhibit at this one</h2>

<p>Most tea trade shows put you in front of the tea trade in general. This one is built around a single corridor — Kenya to China — at a moment when that corridor is unsettled. Kenyan exports to China fell 51% in the first quarter of 2026, while national policy targets a large increase in green and orthodox production and China holds a zero-tariff door open.</p>
<p class="cite">Sources: <a href="https://kenyanwallstreet.com/tea-exports-q1-2026" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">The Kenyan Wall Street</a>, Q1 2026 · <a href="https://www.chinadaily.com.cn/a/202607/21/WS6a5ec8f3a310986e2b466594.html" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">China Daily</a>, 21 July 2026</p>

<p>If you sell into that gap — machinery that moves a producer from bulk black into orthodox, traceability that satisfies a Chinese importer, freight that shortens the route — the people making those decisions are in the building for three days.</p>

